  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "In 1932, Australia waged war against twenty thousand birds\u2014and lost.",
      "words": [
        0,
        9
      ],
      "subject": "major_meredith"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drought drove starving emu hordes into Western Australian wheat farms.",
      "words": [
        10,
        19
      ],
      "subject": "bird"
    },
    {
      "text": "They smashed wooden fences, ruined crops, and left holes for rabbits.",
      "words": [
        20,
        30
      ],
      "subject": "farmer"
    },
    {
      "text": "Desperate wheat farmers begged the government for military protection.",
      "words": [
        31,
        39
      ],
      "subject": "farmer"
    },
    {
      "text": "So the army sent Major Meredith, two gunners, and Lewis machine guns.",
      "words": [
        40,
        51
      ],
      "subject": "major_meredith"
    },
    {
      "text": "They carried ten thousand rounds, expecting easy target practice.",
      "words": [
        52,
        60
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Campion's red dirt, the soldiers set their deadly ambush.",
      "words": [
        61,
        70
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over a thousand giant birds marched toward their hidden trench.",
      "words": [
        71,
        80
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "The gunners waited for point-blank range, then opened rapid fire.",
      "words": [
        81,
        90
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "Suddenly, after just twelve rounds, the gun jammed completely solid.",
      "words": [
        91,
        100
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "The emus didn't freeze; they scattered instantly in ten directions.",
      "words": [
        101,
        110
      ],
      "subject": "bird"
    },
    {
      "text": "Next, the soldiers bolted a Lewis gun onto a rattling flatbed truck.",
      "words": [
        111,
        122
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "They roared across bumpy tracks, chasing sprinting birds at full throttle.",
      "words": [
        123,
        133
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ride was too wild to aim, and an emu smashed their steering gear.",
      "words": [
        134,
        147
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "The truck veered off the road and crashed straight through a fence.",
      "words": [
        148,
        159
      ],
      "subject": "gunner"
    },
    {
      "text": "You see, the emus were fighting organized guerrilla warfare.",
      "words": [
        160,
        168
      ],
      "subject": "major_meredith"
    },
    {
      "text": "Each small squad had a sentinel bird, warning the flock of danger.",
      "words": [
        169,
        180
      ],
      "subject": "bird"
    },
    {
      "text": "Major Meredith admitted the birds could tank bullets like tanks.",
      "words": [
        181,
        190
      ],
      "subject": "major_meredith"
    },
    {
      "text": "After thousands of rounds, the defeated army ordered a full retreat.",
      "words": [
        191,
        201
      ],
      "subject": "major_meredith"
    },
    {
      "text": "In parliament, an MP asked if the soldiers should receive medals.",
      "words": [
        202,
        212
      ],
      "subject": "farmer"
    },
    {
      "text": "Another member replied they should only award medals to the emus.",
      "words": [
        213,
        223
      ],
      "subject": "bird"
    }
  ],
